---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Faceless Pipeline"
  description="Privacy Policy for Faceless Pipeline, a private YouTube upload automation tool."
>
  <div class="container section">
    <span class="section-label">// faceless pipeline</span>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: March 12, 2026</p>

    <div class="prose privacy-prose">
      <div class="highlight-box">
        <strong>Summary:</strong> Faceless Pipeline does not collect any personal data from users.
        It uses Google OAuth solely to upload videos to the owner's own YouTube channels.
      </div>

      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        Faceless Pipeline is a private, server-side automation tool developed and operated by Matt Donders.
        It is not a public-facing application — no end users interact with it. This Privacy Policy
        describes how the application handles Google OAuth credentials and data in order to satisfy
        Google's OAuth app verification requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>Data Collected</h2>
      <p>
        Faceless Pipeline does not collect personal data from any users. The application uses Google
        OAuth 2.0 solely to authenticate requests to the YouTube Data API (<code>youtube.upload</code> scope)
        for the purpose of uploading videos to the owner's own YouTube channels.
      </p>
      <p>No user-facing data is collected, stored, or processed.</p>

      <h2>How OAuth Tokens Are Used</h2>
      <p>
        Google OAuth access and refresh tokens are stored locally on a private, self-hosted server
        controlled by the application owner. These tokens are used exclusively to authenticate
        YouTube Data API upload requests. They are never shared, transmitted to third parties,
        or used for any purpose other than video uploads.
      </p>

      <h2>Data Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        No data of any kind is shared with third parties. The application communicates only with
        Google's YouTube Data API on behalf of the owner's own Google account.
      </p>

      <h2>Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        OAuth tokens are stored on a private server for as long as needed to operate the upload
        pipeline. They can be revoked at any time via
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Google Account permissions settings
        </a>.
        Revoking access immediately invalidates all stored tokens.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        OAuth credentials are stored on a private server with restricted access. They are not
        exposed in any public repository, frontend application, or third-party service.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on
        this page with an updated "Last Updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact:</p>
      <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com">matt@mattdonders.com</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .last-updated {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .privacy-prose h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .privacy-prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .privacy-prose ul {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .privacy-prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .highlight-box {
    background: var(--accent-dim);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .highlight-box strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
